Start the LV2 control ports from the parameters' defaults, not their current values.

An LV2 host's control ports hold the defaults of the TTL until the host sets them, and run()
hands the plug-in every port whose value differs from the last one it saw. Starting that
record from getParameterValue() makes the first run() set every parameter whose current
value is not its default. The SQ8L's parameters are the fields of the program the instance
opened with (src/gui/logic/HostParams.h), whose values are the program's and not the
defaults: the first run() would write the INIT program's values over it. Starting from the
defaults, a port reaches the plug-in only once the host has really set it.

diff --git a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginLV2.cpp b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginLV2.cpp
index d2791951..256b24db 100644
--- a/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginLV2.cpp
+++ b/distrho/src/DistrhoPluginLV2.cpp
@@ -113,7 +113,8 @@ public:
             for (uint32_t i=0; i < count; ++i)
             {
                 fPortControls[i] = nullptr;
-                fLastControlValues[i] = fPlugin.getParameterValue(i);
+                // (SQ8L) what the host's ports hold before it sets them, see the patch
+                fLastControlValues[i] = fPlugin.getParameterDefault(i);
             }
         }
         else
